\par \sect }\sectd \ltrsect\linex0\headery54\footery0\sectdefaultcl\sftnbj \pard\plain \ltrpar\s1\ql \li322\ri0\sb82\nowidctlpar\wrapdefault\nocwrap\nooverflow\faauto\outlinelevel0\rin0\lin322\itap0 \rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af1\afs24\alang1025 \ltrch\fcs0 
\b\fs24\lang1046\langfe1046\loch\af1\hich\af1\dbch\af31505\cgrid\langnp1046\langfenp1046 {\rtlch\fcs1 \af1 \ltrch\fcs0 \lang1033\langfe1046\langnp1033\insrsid15221459\charrsid8994339 \hich\af1\dbch\af31505\loch\f1 Background
\par }\pard\plain \ltrpar\s15\qj \fi707\li322\ri296\sb139\sl360\slmult1\nowidctlpar\wrapdefault\nocwrap\nooverflow\faauto\rin296\lin322\itap0 \rtlch\fcs1 \af1\afs24\alang1025 \ltrch\fcs0 
\fs24\lang1046\langfe1046\loch\af1\hich\af1\dbch\af31505\cgrid\langnp1046\langfenp1046 {\rtlch\fcs1 \af1 \ltrch\fcs0 \lang1033\langfe1046\langnp1033\insrsid15221459\charrsid8994339 \hich\af1\dbch\af31505\loch\f1 
Acute Respiratory Infections (ARI) are a worldwide threat responsible for more than four million deaths annually [1]. The pathogenicity is typically caused by a virus, bacteria, fungi, or a mix of these microorganisms [2]. Although knowledge of modes of t
\hich\af1\dbch\af31505\loch\f1 r\hich\af1\dbch\af31505\loch\f1 
ansmission is ever-evolving, scientific consensus reports airborne transmission by droplets and contact as the main acquisition routes of most respiratory infection diseases, especially viral ARI [1,2].
\par }\pard \ltrpar\s15\qj \fi707\li322\ri294\sb1\sl360\slmult1\nowidctlpar\wrapdefault\nocwrap\nooverflow\faauto\rin294\lin322\itap0 {\rtlch\fcs1 \af1 \ltrch\fcs0 \lang1033\langfe1046\langnp1033\insrsid15221459\charrsid8994339 \hich\af1\dbch\af31505\loch\f1 
According to the World Lung Foundation, mortality rat\hich\af1\dbch\af31505\loch\f1 
es of viral ARI are particularly high in the youngest and oldest people in low- and middle-income nations [1]. In this context, the geographical setting presents itself as a host factor due to the inadequate availability and effectiveness of medical care 
\hich\af1\dbch\af31505\loch\f1 a\hich\af1\dbch\af31505\loch\f1 
nd infection prevention, and control measures of these countries to contain spread, such as vaccines, access to health-care facilities, and capacity of isolation at the hospitals and outpatient settings (or home settings)}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af1 \ltrch\fcs0 
\expnd0\expndtw-2\lang1033\langfe1046\langnp1033\insrsid15221459\charrsid8994339 \hich\af1\dbch\af31505\loch\f1  }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af1 \ltrch\fcs0 \lang1033\langfe1046\langnp1033\insrsid15221459\charrsid8994339 \hich\af1\dbch\af31505\loch\f1 [2].
\par }\pard \ltrpar\s15\qj \fi707\li322\ri294\sl360\slmult1\nowidctlpar\wrapdefault\nocwrap\nooverflow\faauto\rin294\lin322\itap0 {\rtlch\fcs1 \af1 \ltrch\fcs0 \lang1033\langfe1046\langnp1033\insrsid15221459\charrsid8994339 \hich\af1\dbch\af31505\loch\f1 
Due to the high and increasin\hich\af1\dbch\af31505\loch\f1 g incidence and prevalence rates, viral ARI represents an enormous economic burden in healthcare systems, independently of income classification [1\hich\f1 \endash \loch\f1 
3]. To contextualize, an economic burden of diseases is related to the financial loss of individuals, famil\hich\af1\dbch\af31505\loch\f1 i\hich\af1\dbch\af31505\loch\f1 
es, societies, and governments due to economic resources spent related to respond to the diseases [3,4].
\par \hich\af1\dbch\af31505\loch\f1 Outbreaks such as Severe Acute Respiratory Syndrome (SARS) in 2003 [5], and more recently the Coronavirus Disease 2019 (COVID-19) pandemic in December \hich\af1\dbch\af31505\loch\f1 
2019 [6], have shown the burden that viral ARI can inflict in healthcare systems and national economies. In this scenario, valid estimates of the Cost-of-Illness (COI) in different perspectives are of particular importance and necessity to justify prevent
\hich\af1\dbch\af31505\loch\f1 i\hich\af1\dbch\af31505\loch\f1 
ve and intervention-based programs. In the same way, estimates of the overall health system economic impact of viral ARI help to understand what specific factors are driving these costs, and may inform decision-makers to support formulation and refinement
\hich\af1\dbch\af31505\loch\f1  \hich\af1\dbch\af31505\loch\f1 of policies}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af1 \ltrch\fcs0 \expnd-1\expndtw-6\lang1033\langfe1046\langnp1033\insrsid15221459\charrsid8994339 \hich\af1\dbch\af31505\loch\f1  }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af1 \ltrch\fcs0 
\lang1033\langfe1046\langnp1033\insrsid15221459\charrsid8994339 \hich\af1\dbch\af31505\loch\f1 [3,4,7,8].
\par }\pard \ltrpar\s15\ql \li0\ri0\sb1\nowidctlpar\wrapdefault\nocwrap\nooverflow\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\rtlch\fcs1 \af1\afs36 \ltrch\fcs0 \fs36\lang1033\langfe1046\langnp1033\insrsid15221459\charrsid8994339 
\par }\pard\plain \ltrpar\s1\ql \li322\ri0\nowidctlpar\wrapdefault\nocwrap\nooverflow\faauto\outlinelevel0\rin0\lin322\itap0 \rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af1\afs24\alang1025 \ltrch\fcs0 
\b\fs24\lang1046\langfe1046\loch\af1\hich\af1\dbch\af31505\cgrid\langnp1046\langfenp1046 {\rtlch\fcs1 \af1 \ltrch\fcs0 \lang1033\langfe1046\langnp1033\insrsid15221459\charrsid8994339 \hich\af1\dbch\af31505\loch\f1 Objectives
\par }\pard\plain \ltrpar\s15\qj \fi707\li322\ri295\sb137\sl360\slmult1\nowidctlpar\wrapdefault\nocwrap\nooverflow\faauto\rin295\lin322\itap0 \rtlch\fcs1 \af1\afs24\alang1025 \ltrch\fcs0 
\fs24\lang1046\langfe1046\loch\af1\hich\af1\dbch\af31505\cgrid\langnp1046\langfenp1046 {\rtlch\fcs1 \af1 \ltrch\fcs0 \lang1033\langfe1046\langnp1033\insrsid15221459\charrsid8994339 \hich\af1\dbch\af31505\loch\f1 
Our aim is to synthesize the available data on the economic burden of six viral ARI in Upper-Middle-Income Countries (UMIC), highlighting its major causes and comparing direct costs among nations.
\par \sect }\sectd \ltrsect\linex0\headery54\footery0\sectdefaultcl\sftnbj \pard\plain \ltrpar\s1\ql \li322\ri0\sb82\nowidctlpar\wrapdefault\nocwrap\nooverflow\faauto\outlinelevel0\rin0\lin322\itap0 \rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af1\afs24\alang1025 \ltrch\fcs0 
