\b\fs24\lang1046\langfe1046\loch\af1\hich\af1\dbch\af31505\cgrid\langnp1046\langfenp1046 {\rtlch\fcs1 \af1 \ltrch\fcs0 \lang1033\langfe1046\langnp1033\insrsid15221459\charrsid8994339 \hich\af1\dbch\af31505\loch\f1 Data extraction and management
\par }\pard\plain \ltrpar\s15\qj \fi707\li322\ri294\sb138\sl360\slmult1\nowidctlpar\wrapdefault\nocwrap\nooverflow\faauto\rin294\lin322\itap0 \rtlch\fcs1 \af1\afs24\alang1025 \ltrch\fcs0 
\fs24\lang1046\langfe1046\loch\af1\hich\af1\dbch\af31505\cgrid\langnp1046\langfenp1046 {\rtlch\fcs1 \af1 \ltrch\fcs0 \lang1033\langfe1046\langnp1033\insrsid15221459\charrsid8994339 \hich\af1\dbch\af31505\loch\f1 
For data extraction, we will follow a process of two stages. Firstly, two review authors (}{\rtlch\fcs1 \ai\af1 \ltrch\fcs0 \i\lang1033\langfe1046\langnp1033\insrsid15221459\charrsid8994339 \hich\af1\dbch\af31505\loch\f1 
APR and one of ACPNP, FSAR, GFMT or GSR}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af1 \ltrch\fcs0 \lang1033\langfe1046\langnp1033\insrsid15221459\charrsid8994339 \hich\af1\dbch\af31505\loch\f1 ) will extract and compile the data\hich\af1\dbch\af31505\loch\f1 
 of each included study into a prestructured and piloted data collection form, designed specifically for this synthesis. Then, the completed forms will be reviewed by a third review author (}{\rtlch\fcs1 \ai\af1 \ltrch\fcs0 
\i\lang1033\langfe1046\langnp1033\insrsid15221459\charrsid8994339 \hich\af1\dbch\af31505\loch\f1 CRRF}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af1 \ltrch\fcs0 \lang1033\langfe1046\langnp1033\insrsid15221459\charrsid8994339 \hich\af1\dbch\af31505\loch\f1 
) for accuracy and completeness. Discrepancies will be resolve\hich\af1\dbch\af31505\loch\f1 d by discussion and consensus among the authors.
\par }\pard \ltrpar\s15\qj \fi707\li322\ri295\sb1\sl360\slmult1\nowidctlpar\wrapdefault\nocwrap\nooverflow\faauto\rin295\lin322\itap0 {\rtlch\fcs1 \af1 \ltrch\fcs0 \lang1033\langfe1046\langnp1033\insrsid15221459\charrsid8994339 \hich\af1\dbch\af31505\loch\f1 
In the event where there is missing data that we deem important, the corresponding author of the study will be contacted. The process will follow as previously presented for conferences and journals abstract\hich\af1\dbch\af31505\loch\f1 \hich\f1 
 inclusion. If the study fulfills all eligibility criteria but we receive no return within the contact, the label \'93\loch\f1 \hich\f1 Study Awaiting Classification\'94\loch\f1  will be applied}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af1 \ltrch\fcs0 
\expnd-1\expndtw-5\lang1033\langfe1046\langnp1033\insrsid15221459\charrsid8994339 \hich\af1\dbch\af31505\loch\f1  }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af1 \ltrch\fcs0 \lang1033\langfe1046\langnp1033\insrsid15221459\charrsid8994339 \hich\af1\dbch\af31505\loch\f1 [19].
\par }\pard \ltrpar\s15\qj \fi707\li322\ri295\sl360\slmult1\nowidctlpar\wrapdefault\nocwrap\nooverflow\faauto\rin295\lin322\itap0 {\rtlch\fcs1 \af1 \ltrch\fcs0 \lang1033\langfe1046\langnp1033\insrsid15221459\charrsid8994339 \hich\af1\dbch\af31505\loch\f1 
\hich\f1 An initial version of the data collection form will be structured combining general information about the included studies, and elements of the three main \'93\loch\f1 \hich\f1 sets\'94\loch\f1 
 of interest in our review [22]. More specifically, in this version we will extract informatio\hich\af1\dbch\af31505\loch\f1 n\hich\af1\dbch\af31505\loch\f1 
 on: i) study identification (first author and year); ii) type of viral ARI investigated; iii) geographical setting (UMIC); iv) study design; v) study size (e.g. population-based studies or sampled-based studies); vi) population characteristics (e.g. age 
\hich\af1\dbch\af31505\loch\f1 a\hich\af1\dbch\af31505\loch\f1 \hich\f1 
nd gender); vii) epidemiological approach (prevalent or incident); viii) study scope (data source); ix) economic perspective; x) study duration/time horizon; xi) cost components; xii) total cost; xiii) cost conversion (see \'93\loch\f1 \hich\f1 
standardization of cost data\'94\loch\f1 );\hich\af1\dbch\af31505\loch\f1  \hich\af1\dbch\af31505\loch\f1 and xiv) conflicts of interest. Table 1 details the elements of each category and presents}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af1 \ltrch\fcs0 
\expnd-1\expndtw-9\lang1033\langfe1046\langnp1033\insrsid15221459\charrsid8994339 \hich\af1\dbch\af31505\loch\f1  }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af1 \ltrch\fcs0 \lang1033\langfe1046\langnp1033\insrsid15221459\charrsid8994339 \hich\af1\dbch\af31505\loch\f1 definitions.

\par \sect }\sectd \ltrsect\linex0\headery54\footery0\sectdefaultcl\sftnbj \pard\plain \ltrpar\s15\qj \fi707\li322\ri296\sb82\sl360\slmult1\nowidctlpar\wrapdefault\nocwrap\nooverflow\faauto\rin296\lin322\itap0 \rtlch\fcs1 \af1\afs24\alang1025 \ltrch\fcs0 
\fs24\lang1046\langfe1046\loch\af1\hich\af1\dbch\af31505\cgrid\langnp1046\langfenp1046 {\rtlch\fcs1 \af1 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf19\lang1033\langfe1046\langnp1033\insrsid15221459\charrsid8994339 \hich\af1\dbch\af31505\loch\f1 
We will pilot this initial version on a randomly selected sample of included studies (maximum five, if available), and then det\hich\af1\dbch\af31505\loch\f1 ermine the final version. Modifications will be reported in the systematic review publication.

\par }\pard \ltrpar\s15\ql \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\wrapdefault\nocwrap\nooverflow\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\rtlch\fcs1 \af1\afs36 \ltrch\fcs0 \fs36\lang1033\langfe1046\langnp1033\insrsid15221459\charrsid8994339 
\par }\pard \ltrpar\s15\qj \li322\ri0\nowidctlpar\wrapdefault\nocwrap\nooverflow\faauto\rin0\lin322\itap0 {\rtlch\fcs1 \ai\af1 \ltrch\fcs0 \i\cf19\lang1033\langfe1046\langnp1033\insrsid15221459\charrsid8994339 \hich\af1\dbch\af31505\loch\f1 
Standardization of cost data
\par }\pard \ltrpar\s15\qj \fi707\li322\ri294\sb140\sl360\slmult1\nowidctlpar\wrapdefault\nocwrap\nooverflow\faauto\rin294\lin322\itap0 {\rtlch\fcs1 \af1 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf19\lang1033\langfe1046\langnp1033\insrsid15221459\charrsid8994339 
\hich\af1\dbch\af31505\loch\f1 
To reach a better comparability between the different currencies, all reported costs in the included studies will be converted to Purchasing Power Parity (PPP)-adjusted US$ 2021 (Int$ 2021) [20]. For this, we will use the free online cost converter tool f
\hich\af1\dbch\af31505\loch\f1 r\hich\af1\dbch\af31505\loch\f1 om Campbell and Cochrane Economics Methods Group Evidence for Policy and Practice Information and Coordination Centre (CCEMG-EPPI Centre) (https://eppi.ioe.ac.uk/costconversion/) [23].
\par }\pard \ltrpar\s15\qj \fi707\li322\ri295\sl360\slmult1\nowidctlpar\wrapdefault\nocwrap\nooverflow\faauto\rin295\lin322\itap0 {\rtlch\fcs1 \af1 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf19\lang1033\langfe1046\langnp1033\insrsid15221459\charrsid8994339 \hich\af1\dbch\af31505\loch\f1 
When the base year of the currency is not reported or cannot be inferre\hich\af1\dbch\af31505\loch\f1 
d from the manuscript (e.g. last year of data collection), it will be assumed as reference year the year before the publication of the manuscript. For studies presenting estimates for more than one year, the most recent estimate will be extracted. No adju
\hich\af1\dbch\af31505\loch\f1 s\hich\af1\dbch\af31505\loch\f1 tment will be made to economic outcomes expressed as ratios or percentages, e.g. percentage of Gross Domestic Product (GDP) [4].
\par }\pard \ltrpar\s15\ql \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\wrapdefault\nocwrap\nooverflow\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\rtlch\fcs1 \af1\afs36 \ltrch\fcs0 \fs36\lang1033\langfe1046\langnp1033\insrsid15221459\charrsid8994339 
\par }\pard\plain \ltrpar\s1\qj \li322\ri0\nowidctlpar\wrapdefault\nocwrap\nooverflow\faauto\outlinelevel0\rin0\lin322\itap0 \rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af1\afs24\alang1025 \ltrch\fcs0 
\b\fs24\lang1046\langfe1046\loch\af1\hich\af1\dbch\af31505\cgrid\langnp1046\langfenp1046 {\rtlch\fcs1 \af1 \ltrch\fcs0 \lang1033\langfe1046\langnp1033\insrsid15221459\charrsid8994339 \hich\af1\dbch\af31505\loch\f1 Quality assessment
\par }\pard\plain \ltrpar\s15\qj \fi707\li322\ri295\sb139\sl360\slmult1\nowidctlpar\wrapdefault\nocwrap\nooverflow\faauto\rin295\lin322\itap0 \rtlch\fcs1 \af1\afs24\alang1025 \ltrch\fcs0 
\fs24\lang1046\langfe1046\loch\af1\hich\af1\dbch\af31505\cgrid\langnp1046\langfenp1046 {\rtlch\fcs1 \af1 \ltrch\fcs0 \lang1033\langfe1046\langnp1033\insrsid15221459\charrsid8994339 \hich\af1\dbch\af31505\loch\f1 
After extraction, the quality of included studies will be appraised independently by two review authors (}{\rtlch\fcs1 \ai\af1 \ltrch\fcs0 \i\lang1033\langfe1046\langnp1033\insrsid15221459\charrsid8994339 \hich\af1\dbch\af31505\loch\f1 CR
\hich\af1\dbch\af31505\loch\f1 RF and MMCL}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af1 \ltrch\fcs0 \lang1033\langfe1046\langnp1033\insrsid15221459\charrsid8994339 \hich\af1\dbch\af31505\loch\f1 
). Discrepancies will be solved by consensus and, if necessary, a third review author will be consulted (}{\rtlch\fcs1 \ai\af1 \ltrch\fcs0 \i\lang1033\langfe1046\langnp1033\insrsid15221459\charrsid8994339 \hich\af1\dbch\af31505\loch\f1 ANA or VFMT}{
\rtlch\fcs1 \af1 \ltrch\fcs0 \lang1033\langfe1046\langnp1033\insrsid15221459\charrsid8994339 \hich\af1\dbch\af31505\loch\f1 ).
\par }\pard \ltrpar\s15\qj \fi707\li322\ri294\sl360\slmult1\nowidctlpar\wrapdefault\nocwrap\nooverflow\faauto\rin294\lin322\itap0 {\rtlch\fcs1 \af1 \ltrch\fcs0 \lang1033\langfe1046\langnp1033\insrsid15221459\charrsid8994339 \hich\af1\dbch\af31505\loch\f1 
As previously reported, to the best of our knowledge, there is currently no formal guideline or consensus on recommended tools\hich\af1\dbch\af31505\loch\f1 
 or checklists to assess the quality of studies that report the economic burden of diseases [4,7,9]. In our review, we will follow the checklist used by Oliveira, Itria, and Lima [9], that was based on the protocol proposed by the British Medical Journal 
\hich\af1\dbch\af31505\loch\f1 (\hich\af1\dbch\af31505\loch\f1 BMJ) [24], and on the Consolidated Health Economic Evaluation Reporting Standards (CHEERS), version 2013, developed by the International Society for Pharmacology and Outcomes Research (ISPOR)}
{\rtlch\fcs1 \af1 \ltrch\fcs0 \expnd0\expndtw-2\lang1033\langfe1046\langnp1033\insrsid15221459\charrsid8994339 \hich\af1\dbch\af31505\loch\f1  }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af1 \ltrch\fcs0 \lang1033\langfe1046\langnp1033\insrsid15221459\charrsid8994339 
\hich\af1\dbch\af31505\loch\f1 [25].
